WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.205 --> 00:00:07.707
- We live in a universe

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:11.577
where statistically
disorder is king.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:15.048
As time moves forward,
things fall apart.

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:19.085
Stars burn out.
Energy spreads out.

00:00:19.118 --> 00:00:21.654
Entropy conquers all.

00:00:21.687 --> 00:00:25.491
But humans, life, fights
that trend.

00:00:25.524 --> 00:00:27.060
We build things.

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:28.594
We organize things.

00:00:28.627 --> 00:00:31.364
We add information.

00:00:31.397 --> 00:00:36.235
So why is that we love
destroying things?

00:00:36.268 --> 00:00:37.203
[shouts]

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:45.645
Exploding fireworks.

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:48.548
Fights and crashes.

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:50.650
Even popping bubble wrap.

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:52.685
Ugh!

00:00:52.718 --> 00:00:54.754
Tiny cute things can make us

00:00:54.787 --> 00:00:57.090
want to just squeeze 'em
to death.

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:58.792
Ugh!

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.762
Why?

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:05.765
<i> [electronic music]</i>

00:01:05.798 --> 00:01:12.739
<i> ♪ ♪</i>

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:20.813
The power to destroy
is a delicious one.

00:01:20.846 --> 00:01:22.515
Even just holding this here,

00:01:22.548 --> 00:01:24.584
knowing I can drop it,

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:26.385
I am in control.

00:01:26.418 --> 00:01:31.591
I can exert my will in a
dramatic and irreversible way.

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:32.592
Ready?

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:34.127
Ready.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:40.199
<i> ♪ ♪</i>

00:01:40.232 --> 00:01:41.767
Ugh.
[laughs]

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:44.137
Beautiful.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.172 line:0%
Why does that feel so good
to do,

00:01:46.205 --> 00:01:48.374 line:0%
or even just watch?

00:01:48.407 --> 00:01:52.612
For me, throwing it to its death
was almost relaxing,

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:56.315
like I feel calmer now
after being destructive,

00:01:56.348 --> 00:01:59.452
like I've vented
some pent-up energy.

00:01:59.485 --> 00:02:01.621
Or anger?

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:06.259
Why do we like breakings things
when we're angry?

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:08.694
<i> There's a growing trend
 of businesses</i>

00:02:08.727 --> 00:02:11.631
<i>anger rooms that are popping up
 in places</i>

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:14.400
<i> like Texas and Toronto.</i>

00:02:14.433 --> 00:02:16.836
<i> People pay to visit
 these anger rooms</i>

00:02:16.869 --> 00:02:21.374
<i> and let off steam by smashing
 mock-ups of workplaces,</i>

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:23.343
<i> kitchens, and more.</i>

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:30.950
Catharsis Theory proposes
that such acts of destruction

00:02:30.983 --> 00:02:33.186
reduce our anger.

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:34.554
But do they?

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:37.623
Sometimes, but sometimes
they don't.

00:02:37.656 --> 00:02:40.593
This is what makes studying
the mind so difficult.

00:02:40.626 --> 00:02:43.529
Researchers are still looking
into the specifics

00:02:43.562 --> 00:02:47.567
and the variables involved,
and I want to see firsthand

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:51.404
and in person what it's like
when people get angry

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:52.939
and then break things.

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:56.643
Will then be more or less
violent afterwards?

