00:22:13.564 --> 00:22:17.068
<i> Oh, look at that one!</i>

00:22:17.101 --> 00:22:19.637
<i> Don't you just want to hug it
 and squeeze it to--</i>

00:22:19.670 --> 00:22:22.374
<i> well, okay, you get the point.</i>

00:22:22.407 --> 00:22:23.908
<i> ♪ ♪</i>

00:22:23.941 --> 00:22:25.777
<i> To keep things even,</i>

00:22:25.810 --> 00:22:28.046
<i> half of the subjects viewed
 the landscapes first</i>

00:22:28.079 --> 00:22:30.515
<i> and half viewed the puppies
 first.</i>

00:22:30.548 --> 00:22:33.385
<i> But either way, they seemed
 to pop a lot more bubbles</i>

00:22:33.418 --> 00:22:35.787
<i> while watching the puppies.</i>

00:22:35.820 --> 00:22:36.955
<i> Except for this guy.</i>

00:22:39.190 --> 00:22:40.792
[pop]

00:22:40.825 --> 00:22:42.927
<i> ♪ ♪</i>

00:22:42.960 --> 00:22:45.397 line:0%
<i> So-called cute aggression</i>

00:22:45.430 --> 00:22:49.601 line:0%
<i> is a universal
 psychological phenomenon.</i>

00:22:49.634 --> 00:22:51.970
<i> Researchers believe
 the brain's response</i>

00:22:52.003 --> 00:22:54.038
<i>to both cuteness and aggression</i>

00:22:54.071 --> 00:22:56.674
<i> results in the release
 of dopamine</i>

00:22:56.707 --> 00:22:59.077
<i> implicated in the reward
 and pleasure,</i>

00:22:59.110 --> 00:23:02.947
<i> but if we are unable to
 physically touch cute stimuli,</i>

00:23:02.980 --> 00:23:05.683
<i> the desire to do so
 can be regulated</i>

00:23:05.716 --> 00:23:09.554
<i> by substituting aggressive
 physical behavior.</i>

00:23:09.587 --> 00:23:12.690
<i> Will our results reflect
 this theory?</i>

00:23:12.723 --> 00:23:15.060
<i> ♪ ♪</i>

00:23:18.129 --> 00:23:19.864
[laughs]

00:23:19.897 --> 00:23:21.699 align:start position:0%
- How did you feel
about the images that you saw?

00:23:21.732 --> 00:23:23.101
- They were cool.

00:23:23.134 --> 00:23:25.036
- How did you feel about
the puppies?

00:23:25.069 --> 00:23:26.771
- I love them.
- They were very tiny

00:23:26.804 --> 00:23:28.440
and adorable.

00:23:28.473 --> 00:23:30.008
And I wanted to hug them.

00:23:30.041 --> 00:23:32.644
- And how did you feel about
popping the bubble wrap?

00:23:32.677 --> 00:23:36.047 align:start size:78% position:22%
- I felt like I wanted to

00:23:36.080 --> 00:23:38.450 align:start size:72% position:28%
play with the dogs or--

00:23:38.483 --> 00:23:41.619 align:end position:100%
I wanted to play with the bubble
wrap with the dogs.

00:23:41.652 --> 00:23:44.222
<i> - In our simple test, our
 subjects popped an average</i>

00:23:44.255 --> 00:23:48.660
<i> of 33% more bubbles while
 watching cute puppies,</i>

00:23:48.693 --> 00:23:51.496
<i> as opposed to
 boring landscapes.</i>

00:23:51.529 --> 00:23:53.865
- So was the bubble wrap
a stand-in for the puppies?

00:23:53.898 --> 00:23:55.467
- I guess so.

00:23:55.500 --> 00:23:56.935
<i> - In fact, the majority
 of our subjects</i>

00:23:56.968 --> 00:23:59.804
<i> popped more bubbles
 while watching puppies.</i>

00:23:59.837 --> 00:24:02.207
<i> But not this guy.
 Remember him?</i>

00:24:02.240 --> 00:24:05.143 size:84% position:42%
- So how did you feel about
seeing the dog pictures?

00:24:05.176 --> 00:24:08.079 align:end position:100%
- Um, I've always been more
of a cat person.

00:24:08.112 --> 00:24:10.048
<i> - It seems sometimes cuteness</i>

00:24:10.081 --> 00:24:13.017
<i> is a matter of perspective.</i>

00:24:13.050 --> 00:24:16.020
<i> [dramatic music]</i>

00:24:16.053 --> 00:24:18.890
<i> ♪ ♪</i>

00:24:18.923 --> 00:24:22.994
Our relationship with
destruction is not a simple one.

00:24:23.027 --> 00:24:27.966
<i> It can release endorphins
 and relax our minds.</i>

00:24:27.999 --> 00:24:32.904
<i> It can amp us up and make us
 even more aggressive.</i>

00:24:32.937 --> 00:24:36.207
<i> It can even help us regulate
 our emotional reactions</i>

00:24:36.240 --> 00:24:39.210
<i> to cute things.</i>

00:24:39.243 --> 00:24:41.613
Destruction can be useful,

00:24:41.646 --> 00:24:43.681
it can be dangerous,

00:24:43.714 --> 00:24:46.117
and it can be a lot of fun.

00:24:49.287 --> 00:24:51.789
<i> ♪ ♪</i>

00:24:51.822 --> 00:24:54.059
And as always,
thanks for watching.

00:24:59.964 --> 00:25:02.867 line:0%
<i> [electronic music]</i>

00:25:02.900 --> 00:25:09.908 line:0%
<i> ♪ ♪</i>

